-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_lib.pcpp - std compliance: the static C library std_hookio.pcpp
  drives its stream family through

  A `module lib` holding only C: std_hookio_c.c, whose functions read and
  write a file through the stdio stream family (fopen, fread, fseek, ftell,
  the 64-bit seek / tell names, fgetc, getc, ungetc, fgets, fwrite, fputc,
  putc, fputws, the printf family, fscanf on Linux, fflush, fclose, ...).
  std_hookio.pcpp links it (external "std_hookio_lib") and defines the
  HookIO hooks, which must bind the calls inside this archive too. It builds
  and is not run: std_hookio.pcpp holds the output to expect.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\std_hookio_lib.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  CHECK: output\lib holds libstd_hookio_lib.a. Then std_hookio.pcpp.
*******************************************************************************/

module lib std_hookio_lib;
@addsourcefile "$P:res/tests/std_hookio_c.c";

end.
